A NAS message included in the **Replayed NAS message container** IE must:

- Be either an **ATTACH REQUEST** or **TRACKING AREA UPDATE REQUEST** message;
- Be coded **without a NAS security header** (i.e., as a plain NAS message);
- Be formatted according to the specifications in **Clause 8.2.4** (for ATTACH REQUEST) or **Clause 8.2.29** (for TRACKING AREA UPDATE REQUEST);
- Not be a **SECURITY PROTECTED NAS MESSAGE** or **SERVICE REQUEST** message, as these are explicitly excluded per Clause 9.7.

Thus, the message must be a **plain, unsecured** version of the original request message, matching the exact structure defined in the relevant clauses.

A UE configured for eCall only mode shall perform the **eCall inactivity procedure** at the expiry of timers T3444 or T3445. This includes:  
- Stopping other running timers (e.g., T3411, T3412);  
- Performing a detach procedure (EPS-only or combined, depending on current registration state);  
- Deleting stored context (GUTI, TAI list, last visited registered TAI, list of equivalent PLMNs, eKSI);  
- Entering the **EMM-DEREGISTERED.eCALL-INACTIVE** state.  

This applies regardless of the current EMM substate, provided the UE is in EMM-IDLE and not in EMM-REGISTERED.PLMN-SEARCH or EMM-REGISTERED.NO-CELL-AVAILABLE.

The **Negotiated WUS assistance information** IE shall be included in the **ATTACH ACCEPT** or **TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT** message if and only if:

1. The **UE supports WUS assistance** and includes the **Requested WUS assistance information** IE (only when not attaching for emergency bearer services);
2. The **MME supports and accepts the use of WUS assistance** for the UE;
3. The **UE is not attaching for emergency bearer services** (i.e., not in EPS emergency attach or RLOS attach context).

These conditions are mandated by clauses 8.2.1.24 and 8.2.26.27, and are consistent with the WUS assistance capability handling in clause 5.3.21. The network must negotiate and confirm the UE paging probability information only under these non-emergency attach/update scenarios.

The MME shall:

- Set the **EPS update result** IE to **"EPS only"** in the **TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT** message;  
- **Not** indicate **"SMS only"** in the **Additional update result** IE;  
- Include an appropriate **SMS services status** value (e.g., "SMS services not available" or "SMS services not available in this PLMN") in the message;  
- **Not** allocate a TAI list containing both NB-S1 and WB-S1 mode tracking areas (as per Clause 5.5.3.2.4);  
- **Set the EMC BS bit to zero** in the **EPS network feature support** IE (to indicate no emergency bearer service support in NB-S1 mode, if applicable).  

This response aligns with Clause 5.5.3.2.4A and ensures the UE transitions to **EMM-REGISTERED.NORMAL-SERVICE**, resets the tracking area updating attempt counter, stops timer T3430 (if running), and marks the USIM as invalid for SMS services until T3245 expires or the UICC is removed.

The UE includes the Extended DRX parameters IE in an ATTACH REQUEST or TRACKING AREA UPDATE REQUEST message to request the use of extended idle-mode DRX (eDRX), provided that:

- The UE is not performing an attach for emergency bearer services or access to RLOS;
- The UE does not have a PDN connection for emergency bearer services;
- The UE has a valid subscription and the network supports eDRX.

The UE may include the IE in each attach or tracking area updating procedure to maintain eDRX operation, and may resume eDRX after deactivating an emergency PDN connection if the network previously provided eDRX parameters.

The MME shall evaluate the following criteria to conclude that extended protocol configuration options is supported end-to-end for a PDN connection:

- The UE is in NB-S1 mode;  
- The APN requested for the PDN connection is for UAS services;  
- The PDN Type requested is non-IP or Ethernet;  
- OR, the network has indicated support of the extended protocol configuration options IE in the last ATTACH ACCEPT or TRACKING AREA UPDATING ACCEPT message;  
- AND, the network has included the extended protocol configuration options IE in at least one EPS session management message received by the UE for this PDN connection.  

These conditions are derived from Clause 6.6.1.1 of 3GPP TS 24.301.

The primary function of the **Detach type** information element is to **indicate the type of detach** initiated by the UE or network, specifying:  
- Whether the detach is due to **switch off** or not;  
- Whether the detach applies to **EPS services only**, **non-EPS services only**, or **both**;  
- Whether **re-attach is required** or not (i.e., "re-attach required" vs. "re-attach not required").  

This information determines the **procedure behavior**, including signaling flow, state transitions, and whether the UE should re-attach after detach.

When the UE is in EMM-CONNECTED mode and timer T3447 is running, the UE shall not send an UPLINK GENERIC NAS TRANSPORT message unless one of the following conditions is met:  
- The UE is configured to use Access Class 11 (AC11) 15 in the selected PLMN;  
- The UE has a PDN connection for emergency bearer services established;  
- A network-initiated signalling message has been received.  

If the message is still necessary, it may be sent only after timer T3447 expires.  

This restriction is part of the Service Gap Control (SGC) mechanism, where T3447 is used to control the frequency of UE-initiated NAS signalling transitions from EMM-IDLE to EMM-CONNECTED mode.
